WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.002 --> 00:00:12.009
WearAgain combines your wardrobe and a personal stylist. This is the deployed mobile application, using a demonstration profile. The jury page offers installation; compatible phones use the native prompt, and iPhone users get clear instructions.

2
00:00:12.009 --> 00:00:34.015
Start with an empty profile and add your own pieces. Here we enter two tops, trousers, shoes, and a wool top that is in the wash. Clothing photos stay with this profile. Unavailable pieces are excluded from ready-to-wear proposals.

3
00:00:34.015 --> 00:00:48.029
Tell the stylist what you like and what to avoid. We save a no-wool preference, then reload. The memory remains visible and editable. Profiles have separate clothes, photos and decisions; transfer to another device is explicit.

4
00:00:48.029 --> 00:01:08.945
This is a real live request to Sonnet through the Worker. The stylist reads this profile and wardrobe, inspects the enabled garment photo, and proposes complete looks from ready pieces. Paid previews are off. The app verifies item identities before saving the selected outfit.

5
00:01:08.945 --> 00:01:22.946
The saved outfit is made from the same garment records. It survives reload, and the stylist can revise a previous proposal from feedback. The four procedures cover an occasion, a purchase, packing, and rediscovering something rarely worn.

6
00:01:22.946 --> 00:01:42.955
For a purchase, enter your actual needs and a shop candidate. Human pair ratings drive a deterministic minimum-cost certificate. Here the owned shirt already covers the need, so the result is buy nothing. Delivery, stock and size fit are never invented.

7
00:01:42.955 --> 00:02:00.955
In a busy shop, collect garment photos and review the shortlist over coffee. These clearly labelled saved YouCam examples use a built-in model. Mark only the pieces worth returning for. One earlier live Worker render used two credits; this recording starts no new YouCam task.
